[00:08.89]What happened to the clavichord? | 古钢琴怎么了？
[00:12.57]We have an old musical instrument. | 我们有一件古老的乐器。
[00:16.10]It is called a clavichord. | 它被称为古钢琴。
[00:18.91]It was made in Germany in 1681. | 它于1681年在德国制造。
[00:23.78]Our clavichord is kept in the living room. | 我们的古钢琴被放在客厅里。
[00:27.31]It has belonged to our family for a long time. | 它属于我们家已经很长时间了。
[00:31.61]The instrument was bought by my grandfather many years ago. | 这件乐器是我祖父多年前买的。
[00:36.42]Recently it was damaged by a visitor. | 最近它被一位访客损坏了。
[00:39.87]She tried to play jazz on it! | 她试图用它演奏爵士乐！
[00:42.88]She struck the keys too hard and two of the strings were broken. | 她敲击琴键太用力，结果两根琴弦断了。
[00:48.43]My father was shocked. | 我的父亲感到震惊。
[00:51.32]Now we are not allowed to touch it. | 现在我们不被允许碰它。
[00:54.36]It is being repaired by a friend of my father's. | 它正在由我父亲的一位朋友修理。
